## Key Technical Decisions & Trade-offs

### 1. Workflow Representation — Adjacency List in PostgreSQL

- Workflows are stored as **nodes + edges** (not nested JSON)
- Enables querying, versioning, and diffing individual nodes
- **Trade-off**: More complex queries vs. simpler JSON blob storage

### 2. Execution Model — BullMQ Job Chain

- Each workflow execution creates a **root job** in BullMQ
- Each node execution is a **child job** with dependencies
- Nodes with no pending dependencies are auto-promoted
- **Trade-off**: More queue overhead vs. in-process execution (needed for scaling)

### 3. Conditional Branching — Runtime DAG Pruning

- Conditions are evaluated at runtime
- Skipped branches produce "skipped" results (not null)
- Enables the **replay** feature (know exactly which nodes ran)

### 4. Replay — Checkpoint-based Resume

- Each node stores its result + status in PostgreSQL
- On replay, the engine reads existing results
- Skips successful nodes, re-executes from the failed/specified node
- **Trade-off**: Storage overhead vs. instant replay capability

### 5. Webhook Triggers — HTTP Ingress

- Each workflow can register webhook endpoints
- Webhook → creates execution with input data
- Enables integration with external systems

---

## Database Schema

```sql
-- Workflow definition
workflows (id, name, description, active, created_at, updated_at)

-- Version snapshots
workflow_versions (id, workflow_id, version, definition JSONB, created_at)

-- Individual nodes within a workflow
nodes (id, workflow_id, type, config JSONB, position_x, position_y)

-- Connections between nodes
edges (id, workflow_id, source_node_id, target_node_id, source_handle, target_handle)

-- Execution instances
executions (id, workflow_id, version, status, trigger_type, input JSONB, started_at, completed_at)

-- Per-node execution results
node_executions (id, execution_id, node_id, status, input JSONB, output JSONB, error TEXT, started_at, completed_at, attempt)

-- Audit trail
audit_log (id, entity_type, entity_id, action, changes JSONB, created_at)
```

---

## Node Types

| Node Type | Purpose | Complexity |
|-----------|---------|------------|
| **Webhook** | Trigger from HTTP request | Low |
| **HTTP Request** | Call external API | Medium |
| **Condition** | If/else branching | Medium |
| **Transform** | Data mapping/manipulation | Low |
| **Delay** | Wait N seconds | Low |
| **Set Variable** | Store intermediate values | Low |
| **Email** (mock) | Send notification | Low |
| **Database** (mock) | Save/query data | Medium |
| **Code** | Run custom JS snippet | High |
| **Loop** | Iterate over array | High |

---

## API Routes

| Route | Method | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| `/api/auth/register` | POST | Create account |
| `/api/auth/login` | POST | Get JWT |
| `/api/workflows` | GET | List user's workflows |
| `/api/workflows` | POST | Create workflow |
| `/api/workflows/:id` | GET | Get workflow with nodes/edges |
| `/api/workflows/:id` | PUT | Update workflow |
| `/api/workflows/:id` | DELETE | Delete workflow |
| `/api/workflows/:id/activate` | POST | Set active + create version |
| `/api/workflows/:id/versions` | GET | List versions |
| `/api/workflows/:id/execute` | POST | Trigger manual execution |
| `/api/executions` | GET | List executions |
| `/api/executions/:id` | GET | Get execution with node results |
| `/api/executions/:id/replay` | POST | Replay from specific node |
| `/api/webhooks/:workflowId` | POST | Trigger via webhook |

